# Nissan Micra K13 five-door hatchback, 2010-2017.
#
# The fourth-generation Micra: the tall five-door-only body with the large
# oval headlamps sweeping back into the wings, the low body-side crease along
# both doors and the number plate in the bumper below the hatch. The
# pre-facelift car is modelled; the 2013 facelift with its large
# chrome-framed grille is not represented. Nissan sold no three-door K13 and
# no convertible.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nissan_Micra
#
# Dimensions 3.780 x 1.665 x 1.495 m, wheelbase 2.450 m. The published ranges
# run to 3.870 x 1.690 x 1.525 for the 2013 facelift; the pre-facelift UK car
# is at the short, narrow, low end of them.
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is a true level side elevation, but the front
# bumper is cut off at the frame edge, so the nose is taken from images 2 and
# 3, which are a UK Shiro special edition.
#
# Colours: grade (d); no UK colour list was found, although The Telegraph road
# test of 10 October 2010 records ten body colours without naming them. White,
# Red, Blue and Silver are plain names. Weights 12, 10, 9, 8, total 39,
# provisional.
#
# Speed 165 km/h. Comfort 65/428, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 65. Classes 0,1.
# Dates: intro 1 December 2010, the UK on-sale date recorded by a period road
# test; retire 2017, when the K14 replaced it in March.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/nissan-micra-k13.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/nissan-micra-k13.dae. References:
# citycars/references/nissan-micra-k13/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the rear plate is in the bumper, as the photographs
# show, and the headlamp outlines are more angular and narrower than the
# reference. The grille internals and bumper corners are simplified.


